`vul4j_excerpt.csv` is an eight-row excerpt of the Vul4J dataset index, kept here so
`tests/evals/test_harvest.py` can exercise `scripts/harvest_vul4j.py` without the network. It is
not the corpus and nothing reads it at harvest time — `scripts/harvest_vul4j.py` fetches the
live index instead, so that our copy of the dataset cannot silently go stale.

The rows are chosen to cover the cases the harvester has to get right rather than to be
representative: a PoV added by the fix, a PoV present before the fix, a PoV that exists in
neither revision, an abbreviated commit SHA, a commit range, a Vul4J-owned mirror, a covered
CWE, an uncovered one, and a static-analysis entry with no CVE at all.

Source: Vul4J: A Dataset of Reproducible Java Vulnerabilities
        Quang-Cuong Bui, Riccardo Scandariato, et al., MSR 2022
        https://github.com/tuhh-softsec/vul4j
        dataset/vul4j_dataset.csv

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0),
         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Only the dataset is used. Vul4J's own source code is GPL-3.0 and is neither copied nor
adapted anywhere in this repository. Columns Vul4J uses to pin a build environment
(`compile_cmd`, `test_all_cmd`, `test_cmd`, `cmd_options`, `src_classes`, `test_classes`)
are deliberately omitted: see docs/evaluation/CORPUS_SOURCES.md.
